            <ArticleTitle>Pediatric pancreatic pseudocyst: a case report and review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>573-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The differential diagnosis of abdominal pain and mass in children is complicated. An uncommon, but potentially life-threatening cause is pancreatic pseudocyst. The case of a 3-year-old male with a pancreatic pseudocyst is presented. All previously reported cases are reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
